  "factor_name": "Synchronized Cross-Asset Shock Residual Reversal",
  "version": "1.0",
  "calculation": {
    "expression": "I(|mean_cs(sum(return_1d,5))| >= rolling_120d_percentile_80(|mean_cs(sum(return_1d,5))|)) * -(sum(return_1d,5) - 5*cross_sectional_mean_5d_return) / rolling_std(return_1d,40)",
    "description": "When the five-day cross-asset mean move is an extreme synchronized shock, reverse each instrument's five-day return residual versus the cross-sectional mean and scale by trailing 40-day volatility. Inputs are lagged through the completed observation date. The signal is intended for one-day forward returns."
